# The toolchain commits every build here runs on — the SAME ones the ZeroCode AI
# backend builds with, so a green build here means the same thing in the cloud.
# Read by scripts/ci-pin-idf.sh (GitHub Actions checks the public espressif/idf
# image out to IDF_REF at job start), passed to Dockerfile.ci as build args by
# the GitLab image job, and kept in step with the platform's build image.
#
# ESP-IDF master, not a release: ESP32-S31 is an IDF PREVIEW target and exists
# in no tag; e9da155 is the commit esp-matter's README names for it.
IDF_REF=e9da155a72624fce88b8ef2cf3cde9aee2e6067f
# esp-board-manager (github.com/espressif/esp-board-manager): the `idf.py bmgr`
# action + the board packs the board products build against.
BMGR_REF=2beb9b22b0892b343bd555a1ebc9929a7edce8fc
